      "requiresTranslation": false,
      "eventMetadata": {
        "context_description": "SpaceX targets Starship Flight 14 as its first orbital-class mission with V3 vehicles, following the July 24, 2026 Flight 13 splashdown that demonstrated improved upper-stage control. The test would deploy initial V3 Starlink satellites while attempting the first tower catch of the Ship upper stage at Starbase using the Mechazilla arms, with the booster also slated for potential return-to-launch-site recovery. Elon Musk highlighted these goals during the August earnings call, contingent on FAA approval for the expanded profile and orbital trajectory. Recent FCC filings list a possible NET of August 28, though some NASA-linked updates point to early September amid ongoing vehicle stacking and static-fire preparations with Booster 21 and Ship 41. This milestone reflects rapid iteration toward full reusability and higher flight cadence.",
        "context_requires_regen": false,
        "context_updated_at": "2026-08-17T14:32:39.424Z"
      },
      "version": "v1"
