      "eventMetadata": {
        "context_description": "Elon Musk’s July 22, 2026, comments on Tesla’s Q2 earnings call—highlighting growing operational overlap in AI hardware, Terafab semiconductor production, batteries, and Starlink integration with Cybercab—remain the main catalyst sustaining trader interest in a formal Tesla-SpaceX merger. SpaceX’s recent IPO and shared engineering priorities in robotics, energy systems, and autonomous technology have fueled analyst views of an 80-90% likelihood of a 2027 combination, though Musk has deferred formal discussion to proper governance channels. Key uncertainties include China-related regulatory approvals, Tesla’s potential China business separation, and Musk’s differing ownership stakes, which could delay or complicate any announcement despite deepening day-to-day collaborations.",
